From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Remove sudo depmod from modules_install target

In a Nix sandbox build, sudo is not available and depmod cannot run
anyway (no System.map, no writable /lib/modules).  The actual module
installation into INSTALL_MOD_PATH is handled by the kernel build
system when hwpm and modules are invoked with the modules_install goal;
the explicit depmod call here is both unnecessary and broken.

diff --git a/source/Makefile b/source/Makefile
--- a/source/Makefile
+++ b/source/Makefile
@@ -30,7 +30,6 @@ help:
 	@echo   "====================================================================================================================="

 modules_install: hwpm modules
-	@sudo depmod -a

 conftest:
 ifeq ($(MAKECMDGOALS), modules)
